  ],
  "scope": "Explicit Cluster SNI and optional Go certificate-role/alert policy carried to seed/discovered/ASK/MOVED nodes; numeric dial addresses, CA/mTLS checks and default unselected library behavior retained. Application RedisEndpoint opts in, including ordinary no-SNI TLS. Runtime validation required. Optional Sentinel transport-only DNS/TCP/TLS timeout separates socket dialing from Redis setup/read budgets; supplied roots avoid unused blocking native trust lookup. Optional Sentinel socket write timeout guards actual backpressure across write/flush and discards the connection on expiry. Sentinel response timing now begins after the actual request or setup flush, preserving independent read and write budgets. Optional per-node Cluster transport/read/write budgets preserve Sentinel branch options; immediate timeout retries remain in the polled work set. Per-node timeout Cluster keeps a known slot owner as the target during transport recovery and replaces failed write streams before retrying. Managed atomic pipelines can observe only their own deadline while bytes remain pending in poll_write; response loss, flush timeout and earlier in-flight requests cannot inherit that proof."
}
